# The session-grading fixtures are digest-pinned artifacts, not source text.
#
# `include_str!` reads them from the WORKING TREE at build time, so any
# checkout-time line-ending conversion changes the bytes the digest sees. A
# Windows runner with the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrote all 27 lines of
# `contract-cases.jsonl` to CRLF, and the byte-identity assertion — whose whole
# job is proving this file is the copy that was reviewed and leak-gated in
# `cameronsjo/cadence-ecosystem` — failed with a message blaming drift.
#
# `-text` disables every conversion in both directions, so the working-tree
# bytes equal the blob bytes on every platform. Deliberately scoped to these
# two files rather than set repo-wide: a blanket policy would rewrite every
# source file on a Windows checkout to no purpose.
crates/metrics/testdata/grading/* -text
